<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Dries Sept qtr pre-capex net profit falls.</title>
<headline>Dries Sept qtr pre-capex net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-Sept versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit before capital spending     177.47 vs 225.60</p>
<p>    Capital spending			     121.56 vs 136.76</p>
<p>Gold output (kg) </p>
<p>    East Dries-				  4,839.0 vs 5,459.5</p>
<p>    West Dries-				  5,386,1 vs 5,840.0</p>
<p>    Reclamation plant-			   226.5 vs   381.1</p>
<p>Tonnes milled/treated</p>
<p>    East Dries-				537,000   vs 540,000</p>
<p>    West Dries-				622,000   vs 638,000</p>
<p>    Reclamation plant-		     562,000   vs 584,000</p>
<p>Yield(gram/t)</p>
<p>    East Dries-				    9.0   vs    10.1</p>
<p>    West Dries-				    8.7   vs    9.2</p>
<p>Full name: Driefontein Consolidated Ltd, managed by Gold</p>
<p>Fields of South Africa Ltd.</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said that following weeks of labour unrest</p>
<p>at the mine, the situation had begun normalising from September</p>
<p>19. Production should increase in the forthcoming quarter and</p>
<p>with the rehabilitation of the 34 line longwall an improvement</p>
<p>in yield was expected.</p>
<p>Fires at East Dries also contributed to poor operating</p>
<p>results.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
